# Benji (bouyonmusique.com, wave 3 parity, 2026-10-20)
# Sources used:
# - TK International, official band site, About Us page (opened 2026-10-20): Wayne “Mr. Benji N’O” Benjamin listed as frontline vocalist with David “Sonic Tazzy” George and Lennan “Ticky” Matthew; Benji produced and sang lead on “Log On” on the Fanatik era, returned as guest in 2004 and produced the title track of Sewo, full member by 2005, after which Triple Kay repertoire reflected the bouyon genre for which Benji was known; Benji raspy chants described; band albums, road march titles, “Heat”, “Toufe”, “Whistle”, Meritorious Service Award 2022 and Golden Drum Award 2022 for the band.
# - eMAGE DM, January 27, 2021 (opened 2026-10-20): Wayne Benjamin, Mr. Benji N2O, of the Triple Kay Band, named Cultural Ambassador of Dominica by the Government of Dominica, appointment effective February 1; front man of a band that dominated the bouyon scene for over a decade; quotes from Benji and from Minister Edward Registe on mentorship of youth and the underprivileged, Fond Cole Development Committee and Roseau City Council membership.
# - Writeups24, January 28, 2021 (opened 2026-10-20): Cabinet approved Wayne “Benji” Benjamin as Cultural Ambassador of the Commonwealth of Dominica, effective February 1, 2021; lead vocalist of Triple Kay International; first runner up in a 2009 competition held in St Kitts and Nevis (competition not named in the article, so none is named here).
# - Soca News, May 16, 2022 (opened 2026-10-20): Triple Kay originating from Laudat, nine members, frontline trio Sonic Tazzy, Mr Benji N’O (Wayne Benjamin) and Ticky; music spans cadence-lypso, Haitian compas, zouk and bouyon; WCMF crowd favourites; album list Big Ting (2000) to Bubblin (2012); 2022 songs Riddim In Your Blood, One Call Away and One Melody.
# - A Virtual Dominica, Bouyon in Dominica page (opened 2026-10-20): Triple Kay together since 2000, albums Big Ting, Fanatik, Sewo, All Out, Pressure and Colours (2008); Band of the Year 2004 and 2005, Song of the Year “Sewo” in 2005; Wayne “Mr. Benji N2O” Benjamin, lead vocalist, recognised as Best Male Artist of the Year at the 2005 Flamboyant Awards; 2008 People Road March with “Please”.
# - ItzCaribbean, Benjai artist page (search result, 2026-10-20): Benjai is a different artist, a soca artist born Rodney Le Blanc in Trinidad and Tobago. Cited only to separate Benji from Benjai; no Benjai fact is attributed to Benji.
# Note on spelling: sources write the stage suffix two ways, N2O (eMAGE DM, A Virtual Dominica) and N’O (TK International, Soca News). This profile prints both spellings as published and does not choose between them. No verified birth date, hometown beyond the Dominica and Roseau public roles documented below, solo album or official personal social URL was confirmed, so none is printed and sameAs is empty. All band recordings in the schema are Triple Kay recordings on which Benji is a frontline vocalist, not solo Benji singles, and the profile says so.

